Row action buttons: the same gap as every other row of buttons

Table rows put their actions side by side 4px apart, half the 8px (--sp-2) that the
theme uses between buttons everywhere else: the Save bar, dialog footers, page and
section headers. Beside the ⋯ menu that a row with three or more actions folds into
(Network > Interfaces: Edit and ⋯), the narrow gap made Edit and ⋯ read as one
split button, and looked out of step with the buttons around them.
Row actions now use --sp-2 too. Nothing else changes: the columns stay right-aligned,
and the phone layout, where a row's buttons wrap, inherits the same gap.

Applies to: https://github.com/anothaDev/luci-theme-vantage.git @ v1.2.0 (a7ff63b7), after 0001, 0002 and 0003.
Upstream status: local to CleanWRT.

